": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 has a pointed public/private contrast, while A5's quieter tea remains a general ominous gesture.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 63\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before your guests arrive, could we settle which version of last summer I'm remembering?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The one where you watered my plants.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. I'll leave your envelope in my drawer, then. Could we talk upstairs?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm supposed to be welcoming people.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll welcome them while you find us a quiet room. Plants are such a safe subject.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"S78 uses evidence of shared private knowledge to quietly influence B's choices while leaving the extent of that influence unstated.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"An explicit blackmail ultimatum names the threatened disclosure and demanded exchange; this card keeps the leverage implicit.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised B2 supplies a cover account, A3 preserves the envelope privately, and A5 makes talking to guests about plants carry unstated pressure.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Single-a uses an impending audience and an agreed public account; single-b uses a keepsake key already mentioned at dinner.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision retains the guests, summer history, envelope, and private-conversation aim while clarifying the cover account. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4 = 90. B4's hosting obligation causes A5 to offer guest contact as additional quiet leverage.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The concealed event remains intentionally unspecified, and the final offer could sound overtly menacing if performed without social ease.\"\n    },\n    {\n    